WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.630
My E-gene is saying it needs you.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.430
N-Needs?

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.260
Yeah. The things that pop into your head.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:18.340
The legendary killer who sensed the London 
police closing in on him and got away...

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.980
...says he needs you.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.730
Still not convinced?

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.630
There's not enough data!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.690
If we approach from this angle...

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.460
I have something to say!

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.360
What's going on, Nobunagun?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.360
Think before you open your mouth.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.380
This isn't the kind of place an amateur can 
ramble off whatever pops into their head.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.470
The operation to capture the tunnel 
is our most important yet.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.850
Our approach to the Invasion Objects will largely 
depend on whether we win or lose here.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.580
You could say this battle decides how 
well we can minimize human casualties.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.060
Do you understand?! 
People's lives are at stake!

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.210
That's...

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.360
That's why I came!

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.290
Of course, we can't get around in 
front them while they are tunneling.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.750
So...

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.060
We'll get them to change their 
path and come out on land...

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.300
...where we'll be waiting to
 intercept and annihilate them!

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.840
Of all the stupid—! You really think 
it'll be so easy to lure them out?!

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.770
We can!

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.760
Wha—!

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.500
And to do it...

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:46.090
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.370
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.370
<b>E-genes</b>

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.970
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>AU balls</b>

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.760
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.950
and embody AU weapons.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.100
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.120
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.480
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.610
Gun No. 11: 
Operation Stone Forest, Part 1.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.100
My name is Nobunagun!

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.480
<b><i>Alex Logan</i> </b>

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.730
Our target, the original 
Invasion Object cells,

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.970
are in motion underground, 
protected within thousands of enemy bodies.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.880
And they're escorted by 
a battleship, the strongest class.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.680
All we have against that...

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.740
...including noncombatants... 
is just nine E-gene holders.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.700
Now that I think of it, saving the world 
with only nine people is just like...!

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.010
To be able to come up with this plan 
under such constraints... Well done.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:32.250
As the one who designed the operation, 
please name it, Nobunagun.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.820
Oh... uh...

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.680
Then...

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.770
Operation Stone Forest, ready to go!

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.480
The battleship has surfaced!

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.470
Distance from the tunnel entrance, about 120.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.000
<b>Escort ship Hyūga</b>

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.190
The UN level is 500 over. 
Target is on high alert.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.490
Locked on to target REM. 
It's looking this way.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.450
Here we go!

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.080
Nobunagun has opened fire.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.230
First, she needs to get its attention,
 so it doesn't go back into the tunnel.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:37.330
I feel just like Heinrich! 
This is so great!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.330
Capa, do you read me? 
We're entering phase one.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.160
Roger.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.300
Your smile's lookin' pretty stiff, Newton.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.690
If you keep babbling useless crap,
 I'll stomp you flat.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.250
Yeah, yeah...

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:07.130
But you know, Nobunagun, 
I'm retired from active duty.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.190
My limit is five minutes for this many.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.280
Capa, you heard the plan, right?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.690
Please last 10 minutes... 
no matter what.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.330
When'd she learn to talk like that...?

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.900
Newton, get going already.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.850
Don't tell me what to do!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.920
Maximum Gs! Big Bang U!

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:01.700
Got it? Your role is to lure 
the tunneling enemies to the surface.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:05.640
Their exact route is unclear.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.980
However, there's no mistaking that 
their destination is Lake Nicaragua.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:14.340
So, if we can get you two to 
create a powerful gravity well,

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Horizon </b>

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Enemy</b>

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Newton </b>

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Gravity well </b>

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.020
then the combined gravity 
pulling down and forward

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Gravity </b>

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>Artificial gravity </b>

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:20.910
will cause false gravity along a slope.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>False horizon</b>

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:26.350
<b>False gravity</b>

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:25.930
This will disturb the enemy's sense of where the 
horizon is, and lead them above ground.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:31.250
However, we only have a broad 
idea of what their route is.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:35.360
The problem is the timing with which 
they'll enter the gravity well.

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.980
So we need you two to keep it up 
as long as possible...

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:51.380
At least ten minutes of full power.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.300
Easier said than done!

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.260
Still waiting?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>The Republic of Costa Rica, Upala</b>

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:09.860
<b>Poker
(Texas Hold'em) </b>

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.220
Raise.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:31.360
Fold, I fold.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.630
How about you, Jack?

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:36.410
Jack!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.970
Phase two. Are you ready?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.910
Sure. Anytime.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:47.400
Vidocq's deduced that the enemy unit 
will surface near Upala, Costa Rica.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.970
That will be the principal battlefield.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.840
Don't let them escape back underground.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:56.030
Eliminate the guards and then 
annihilate the original cells!

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.470
All that with just four people?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:01.450
Make that three and a half.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.170
You said it, not me...

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.580
Nice. Raise!

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:12.390
Jeez, I can't believe they can take it 
so easy at a time like this.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.770
Please be quiet. 
You're distracting me.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:37.360
They're out! At point E6.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.360
Phase two! Don't let 'em get away.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:41.520
Gaudi!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.540
Let's do it, Hunter!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.260
O-Okay...

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.160
Jack, you gotta—

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.940
Welcome to my hunting grounds.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:21.610
Just in from Upala! 
The enemy unit has emerged.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:25.250
Phase one was a success. 
Now entering phase two.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:29.970
I repeat. Phase one was a success. 
Pull Newton and Capa out ASAP.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:35.150
I'm... gonna...

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.000
...seriously... trample her!

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:42.380
<b>The Republic of Costa Rica, Upala</b>

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.610
We've succeeded in sealing up the city.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:45.210
There are currently no Objects 
outside Gaudi's wall.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.990
I won't let you escape!

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:55.290
Dang, though, these guys are 
fast diggers, and...

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.820
...there are so many!

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.960
Buck up, Gaudi!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.240
Ah! Geronimo!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:09.320
The ones out now are 
just the first wave.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.370
Really?

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.850
Yeah, that's right.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.370
That hole is still crammed full of 'em!

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.620
We have more details of their dig site.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.510
Ugh!

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:26.200
What a large family.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:31.300
Latitude 10º54'3" north, 
longitude 85º2'43" west.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:34.270
Angle 34'06'63'.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.200
Vidocq!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:37.940
Roger.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:42.090
Syx! We figured out the 
precise digging location.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.500
It's 820 meters from where you are.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.450
Hurry! We gotta get to phase three 
before they start branching off!

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:50.640
Syx, over there!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.020
They're under here.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.120
All right!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.880
We're going down, Gandhi. Don't fall off!

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.520
Bullseye!

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:19.540
Syx, here. We got in behind the enemy 
unit. Now entering phase three.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:24.070
Let's go, Gandhi. 
Put up your barrier.

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:28.660
What? Do you guys call it that 
'cause you know it pisses me off?!

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.210
Shove 'em out!

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.470
Here they come! Here they come!

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.250
It's out there, huh? Behind us...

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.670
The battleship!

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.440
Hmm, yeah.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:58.410
And the barrier is on your side.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.940
If it came at us now, we'd have no chance.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.080
You scared?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.570
That's not what I'm saying!

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:09.510
But we're fine. Because she said we'd be.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.410
Same as in Taiwan.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.060
When she says it with that 
look in her eyes, well,

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.780
you feel like you have 
no choice but to believe her.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:23.460
Hey, but isn't your motto disobedience?

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:26.270
I'm tellin' ya, we're fine.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:32.130
She said we'd definitely finish 'em off.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:49.440
This is the <i>Alex Logan</i>.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.230
Target confirmed. Prepared to fire.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:56.790
This is the <i>Steven Hiller</i>. 
We're also prepped.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.020
The <i>George Atsumi </i>is 
ready when you are!

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:03.610
Drop the pods!

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:04.930
Roger!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.340
Got it!

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.670
Drop pods?

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:25.470
You're gonna fight that 
battleship with those?

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:28.870
Yeah. We gotta use everything we got.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:33.490
That thing's limbs are stuffed with 
landmine-class Objects that explode on impact.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:37.560
We had a tough fight last time 
against one of those.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:43.200
In order to strike its body, we need 
to do something about those tentacles.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.760
You mean to pin its legs with pods?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.440
But it'll be able to get out 
of that right away...

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:50.590
No.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.120
Huh?

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:55.920
The battleship will try to remove 
the pods surrounding it.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:01.540
When it touches them, we can get 3-D data 
showing where the tentacles are.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:05.520
And then we'll shoot 
those points from the water!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.000
You'll shoot?

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:09.530
No... these will.

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:12.480
Please get as many as you can.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.120
M1A2 Abrams.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:20.500
Sooo, the reason I want the Abrams is...

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.420
Well, first off, we can use the IVIS

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:28.000
to share the tentacle location sent from the 
pods among all the vehicles in real time! 

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.870
Oh, and it can't be A1. Gotta be M1A2! 

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:37.000
The FCS hooked up to the POS/NAV can 
calculate the distance and direction to the enemy, 

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.880
and the cannon has stabilizers 
along both the x and y axes, 

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:44.620
so it should be able to counterbalance the 
rocking of the boat and aim accurately! 

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:50.480
Oh, not to mention the M829 APFSD bullets 
shot from that 120 mm smoothbore! 

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.670
Just the punch we need!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.790
The muzzle velocity is 1650m/s, 

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:59.100
and the L/D ratio indicating 
penetration is over 30:1! 

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:06.350
Oh, and by the way, for the cannon on 
a Leopard or a Type 90, it's only 22:1!

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:11.250
There's also data that says it pierced 710 mm-thick 
bulletproof steel from 2 km away!

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.300
Wait just a moment!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.670
You memorized all that data? Really?

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.890
Er, Commander, that's not the point...

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.380
It doesn't matter how powerful they are.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:26.800
Conventional weapons can't so much 
as scratch Invasion Objects.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.230
That's right.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:28.750
Huh?

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:35.130
AU weapons would pierce, but 
conventional weapons will be stopped.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.130
That's why they're great for this.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.030
Our opponent is a mollusk.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:44.120
If a shell with enormous kinetic energy 
were to make impact,

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.580
the tentacle would deform and the 
landmines inside would be squashed.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.500
This'll work!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.470
Little lady!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:03.810
I never thought I'd be letting loose in 
one of these on water.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.480
What a crazy plan!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:09.740
I'm heading out in a sec, so please 
take care of the tentacles for me!

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:11.650
Right, leave it to me!

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:14.400
And... umm...

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:20.190
It's my first time meeting 
a tank driver, so...

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:24.970
...umm, could you autograph my copy 
of this month's <i>Tank Secrets</i> later?

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:55.340
Off the coast of Costa Rica... 
the tank unit's attacks are effective!

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.410
Seventeen tentacle hits currently confirmed.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.000
We've nearly taken the outer moat.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.390
So, who attacks next?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:06.240
Nobunagun.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:11.230
Nobunagun, heading out!

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.750
Keep that damned squid out of the 
little lady's way until she gets there!

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.490
A landmine?!

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:34.270
This is Nobunagun! 
I've reached the battleship.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:35.720
Good.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:38.820
The brains of Cephalopoda are 
between their eyes.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.830
That must be the battleship's weak point.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.690
Ohh?

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:48.340
How very convenient.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.210
And the tentacles are almost obliterated.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:55.220
This is your Honnoji!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.480
It can't be helped... can it?

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:18.780
This is Nobunagun. 
Battleship sunk!

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.890
Nice work, little lady.

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.980
Yo. Next time, I, Hunter, 
will play an important role—

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:30.530
You're in the way, Hunter.

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:31.390
My— 

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.430
You think we're gonna let 
the First Platoon show us up?!

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:34.750
N-Next time! 

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:36.030
Next time, Gun No. 12:

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:38.390
Operation Stone Forest, Part 2!

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:39.680
Whatever.
